WEBVTT

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:05.600
I see. Aoi-dono's gone.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.710
Yes. I'm the master now.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:11.260
That must be hard for you.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.410
The previous employee 
seems to be gone now, too.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.410
Previous? Do you know something?

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:22.260
I only heard Aoi-dono mention him.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.870
Before he became an employee...

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:31.900
He was a dangerous fellow who 
killed and imprisoned yokai.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:36.720
But I only heard about it after he was gone.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.090
I'm glad you're the master now, Itsuki.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.930
Let me introduce you.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:45.600
This is Chunichi.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.990
This is Chunji.

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:48.380
This is Chunzo.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:49.600
This is Chunyon.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.480
And this is Chungo.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.580
Who's who?

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:57.560
All five of 'em have 
finally grown this large.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:00.330
Before, I wouldn't exorcise 
them because I thought

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:04.040
they wouldn't be able to acclimate
to the change in environment,

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.620
but now there's no problem at all.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:11.690
Oh, good! This'll be a load off my shoulders.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:13.010
Hear that, boys?

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:15.110
You're going to the Underworld.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:56.320
<b>Mystery 11 "The Return"</b>

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.660
We should get ready.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:55.630
Oh, I forgot to mention that

00:02:55.630 --> 00:03:00.200
only four of the five brothers have made 
preparations to go to the Underworld.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:05.530
Chungo doesn't need to be 
exorcised. He's not ready yet.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.400
What preparations?

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:10.540
<i>He has a crescent pattern. 
That'll be easy to remember.</i>

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.540
He's the only one who still can't fly.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:18.320
But you can walk to the Underworld.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:20.460
There shouldn't be a problem exorcising him.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:22.270
I know that.

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:27.260
But if he can't keep up with his 
brothers in the Underworld,

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:28.650
he'll hold them back.

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:32.510
I see.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:36.270
But it'd be sad to leave 
just one brother behind.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:39.070
He doesn't seem to be 
smaller than his brothers.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:43.070
Is there some other problem, 
such as the way he flies?

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:48.250
If I knew, I could teach him.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:52.440
I told them they couldn't be exorcised 
until they learned to fly.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:55.460
I've been making them practice every day.

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:58.330
His brothers could fly right away,

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:02.080
but for some reason, Chungo falls 
immediately when he tries.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:05.800
At this rate, there's no telling 
when he'll learn to fly.

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:07.320
Komon-dono.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:13.230
Could you show me how they fly?

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:16.120
Shall we head to our usual 
practice area, then?

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:17.450
Practice area?

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:24.530
Abeno-san!

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.840
Can you hear me?

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:30.040
I'm ready!

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:34.950
His voice easily reaches 
the bottom of the ravine.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:36.840
What is he, a siren?

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:39.000
Can you hear me?

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.490
If you can hear me, wave your hand!

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:47.040
Go ahead and start practicing!

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:51.100
I had them practice flying up to the bridge.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:54.280
Unlike the top of the cliff, 
there's no wind here.

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:55.230
Wind?

00:04:55.720 --> 00:05:00.010
It's the perfect place to practice 
flying without being blown around.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:06.380
The bridge is swaying!

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:09.640
I'm scared, I'm scared, I'm scared!

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:12.600
It seems to be gusty up there.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:16.040
Be careful not to get blown away.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.050
Chungo-dono, you as well.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:37.690
Is he serious?

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:47.360
Why don't we start by practicing flapping?

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:52.620
Abeno-san is flapping...

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:54.900
Good grief.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:58.170
Looks like he still can't fly.

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:01.260
<i>I guess, like Komon-san said,</i>

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:04.540
<i>we'll just have to exorcise 
the brothers separately.</i>

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:09.000
<i>I doubt Chungo-san wants to be left behind.</i>

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.760
<i>I hope he learns to fly soon.</i>

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.770
Boys, hold on tight!

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:17.180
The wind's blowing!

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:23.730
Boys!

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:26.490
Oh, right.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:31.050
They've all learned to fly.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:35.640
<i>I'm glad Chungo wasn't up here.</i>

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:38.110
Whoa!

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:39.500
Komon-san!

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:58.460
Abeno-san, help!

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:00.100
Huh?

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:03.930
The crescent pattern?

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:10.280
Huh?

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:12.160
Chungo!

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:15.780
Chungo's flying!

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:22.920
Could someone who couldn't even flap his 
wings a moment ago suddenly be able to fly?

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.750
"You can't go to the Underworld 
unless you learn to fly."

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:28.760
I knew it.

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:32.180
So that's what that meant.

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:40.090
Be careful you don't take 
too good care of them.

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:46.920
Abeno-san?

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:52.360
Hey! Stop fighting!

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:58.570
What are they arguing about?

00:07:58.570 --> 00:08:02.160
I don't understand them, either.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:03.320
Abeno-san?

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.150
I don't know, either.

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:08.630
But I know more or less why they're fighting.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:13.230
It's because Chungo-dono was 
pretending he couldn't fly.

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:14.340
What?!

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:18.140
What? Is that true, Chungo?

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:24.040
But you're the one most bothered 
by your inability to fly.

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:26.400
Why were you pretending you couldn't?

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:30.170
Probably because Chungo-dono 
thought he could stay

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:32.490
in the mundane world if he couldn't fly.

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:38.950
Be careful you don't take 
too good care of them.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:43.880
Aoi-dono told me to be careful

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:47.280
not to take too good care of them.

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:51.780
I never quite knew what 
that meant, but now I do.

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:55.480
It seems that I took too good care of them

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:58.470
and made the mundane world 
a comfortable place to be.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:01.060
Comfortable, huh?

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:06.840
<i>Komon-san watched over them 
well, but it backfired.</i>

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:15.460
All right, I've decided.

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:18.200
I'll abandon my home and move.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:19.910
Move?

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:23.610
Without this home, they'll 
have no place to return to.

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:26.740
Then they'll have to go to the Underworld.

00:09:27.430 --> 00:09:29.500
There's no time like the present.

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:31.480
I'd like to get packed 
up as soon as possible,

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:33.720
so lend me a hand, Mononokean.

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:39.720
Go faster.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:43.140
Okay, I get it! Stop pushing me!

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:47.290
Don't toss things off the cliff!

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:50.860
What? But that's what I always do.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:54.360
Humans have rules for disposing of garbage?

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:56.980
How inconvenient.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:02.920
<i>Their gazes are killing me.</i>

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:05.570
<i>This is where they grew up, after all.</i>

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:09.240
<i>I know it's hard to watch it be 
destroyed, but we have no choice.</i>

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:11.320
What's this?

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:14.380
Now, that brings back memories!

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.080
So that's where it's been.

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:17.920
Komon-san, do you wear this?

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:20.570
Not me, the boys.

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:21.870
Before I built my nest,

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:24.930
I kept them inside it so they 
wouldn't get blown away by the wind.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:31.900
Oh? Looks like you boys remember, too.

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:33.820
They love it.

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:36.090
I'll hold on to this instead 
of throwing it away.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:38.940
No, we're throwing it out.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:43.940
I don't need it anymore.

00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:53.350
<i>I'll secretly give it to them later.</i>

00:10:53.350 --> 00:10:55.550
Ashiya, what time is it?

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:59.800
It's, uh... 4:32.

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:01.990
That late already?

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:05.680
We won't be able to see soon.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.490
That'll make walking dangerous.

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:11.720
Komon-dono, since the 
sun is starting to set,

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:14.440
this is as late as we can help you.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.380
We should exorcise them to the Underworld.

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:18.090
Or...

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:21.020
Would you prefer to stay here?

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:33.800
I don't know what he's saying,

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:36.350
but it looks like he wants 
to go to the Underworld now.

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:37.380
Yeah.

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:39.380
Sorry for all the trouble.

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:42.310
Please go ahead, Mononokean.

00:11:46.070 --> 00:11:49.170
Master of the Mononokean, Abeno Haruitsuki,

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:51.270
requesting a portal to the Underwor—

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:57.450
Abeno-san! Did you forget 
that we're on top of a cliff?

00:11:57.450 --> 00:12:00.590
In any case, crawl back up!

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:03.600
Oh, boy... Now I've done it.

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:04.860
Done what?

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:08.660
I failed to open the portal.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:13.530
That was once. Next time will be twice.

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:17.180
We wouldn't want you to lose 
consciousness and collapse.

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:18.860
Let's go somewhere else.

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:23.880
Welcome to the Mononokean!

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:26.080
This place hasn't changed.

00:12:26.080 --> 00:12:28.740
This reminds me of the last time you came.

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:31.890
The four and a half mats 
feel larger than normal.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:34.240
Komon-dono, please come in.

00:12:34.240 --> 00:12:35.900
Uh, yeah...

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:38.400
I'm not going.

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:41.360
Komon-san?

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:46.080
I need to decide where I'm sleeping 
tonight before it gets dark.

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:50.200
Why not stay here, if it's just for tonight?

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:56.460
I'll find someplace to sleep if
I start looking now, so don't worry.

00:12:56.460 --> 00:13:00.720
Besides, I decided for myself that 
when I set foot in the Mononokean,

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:05.200
it will be when I'm exorcised 
to the Underworld.

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:08.470
I'll see them off from here.

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:21.820
Thank you!

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:21.820
Love you!

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:21.820
Take care!

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:21.820
Love you!

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:24.190
Goodbye.

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:34.950
"Sorry I pretended I couldn't fly."

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:39.040
That's what he seems to be saying.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:43.340
Sorry I pretended I couldn't fly!

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:43.340
Our translator's capabilities 
seem rather suspect,

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:46.520
but I believe they're 
more or less on the mark.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:52.350
I see. I'm relieved I finally 
got to see you fly.

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:56.100
Now I can see you off 
without any worries.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:14:00.970
Chunichi, Chunji, Chunzo, Chunyon, Chungo...

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:05.870
On this day, I'm watching all 
five of you leave the nest.

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:08.110
You've all graduated from my care.

00:14:11.090 --> 00:14:12.250
Bye, now.

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:24.320
Since Abeno-san messed 
up summoning a portal,

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:26.090
this will be his second time today.

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:26.760
Roger that.

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:32.760
Mononokean, take us to 
the roof of the school.

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:38.770
Got it.

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:48.400
They're apologizing for 
fighting with their brothers.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:54.410
Chungo-san messed it up, but they 
came up with the plan together.

00:14:55.510 --> 00:14:57.340
Together?

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:04.500
Abeno-san.

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:05.530
Huh?

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:08.740
I know the real reason he 
pretended he couldn't fly.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:15.010
When they first started practicing how 
to fly, they made the decision together

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:20.270
to leave just one of them with Komon-san.

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:22.520
Why?

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:25.960
Because Komon-san loves them.

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:27.800
To thank him for taking them in,

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:30.780
they wanted to give one of 
them to him as a present.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:34.140
Give a brother as a present?

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:36.200
But since they couldn't 
communicate with him,

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:39.900
one of them pretended he couldn't fly 
so he could stay in the mundane world.

00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:42.260
The Mononokean translated for me.

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:44.920
But...

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:53.410
"If Komon-san is happier alone, 
then she doesn't need me."

00:15:53.410 --> 00:15:59.020
"Komon-san seems to prefer to 
live alone rather than with us."

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:02.690
"If that's the case, I'll go with my 
brothers to the Underworld."

00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:05.260
...is apparently their explanation.

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:07.070
So?

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:08.870
So? So, what?

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:14.190
You're going to the Underworld 
because Komon-dono told you to,

00:16:14.190 --> 00:16:17.620
but were willing to stay here because you all decided that together.

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:19.660
How do you actually feel?

00:16:23.030 --> 00:16:25.670
Do you want to go to the 
Underworld with your brothers,

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:27.270
or...

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:32.920
Let's go home, Itsuki.

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:37.930
Do you want to go home to Komon-dono?

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:21.320
Looks like he's heading back to Komon-san.

00:17:21.320 --> 00:17:22.140
Yeah.

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:25.980
Do you think Komon-san will 
make a complaint later?

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:28.570
She said she wanted to live alone.

00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:32.570
Maybe, but...

00:17:41.270 --> 00:17:46.520
If she was just pretending that was 
what she wanted, I'm not so sure.

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:21.390
It seems that I took too good care of them

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:24.680
and made the mundane world 
a comfortable place to be.

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:41.350
<i>He's right. I'm sure everyone...</i>

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:57.820
<i>prefers a companion over being alone.</i>

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:06.540
<i>"We planned to exorcise the five 
yokai living with the client,</i>

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:10.730
<i>but one of them remained in the mundane 
world and returned to the client."</i>

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:16.550
That must be hard for you.

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:20.300
The previous employee 
seems to be gone now, too.

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:21.910
Mononokean.

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:27.160
Was there ever a human employee before me?

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:30.310
No. You're the only human employee.

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:33.810
Komon-dono must've been confused.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:41.280
Before he became an employee,

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:46.120
he was a dangerous fellow who 
killed and imprisoned yokai.

00:19:55.010 --> 00:19:56.630
Welcome back.

00:19:57.730 --> 00:20:00.010
What does that expression mean?

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:02.870
Did you injure yourself again?

00:20:04.020 --> 00:20:06.300
This is more convenient for me.

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:09.160
Once you realized you could 
blow off work, you couldn't stop.

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:12.060
At least it's not my dominant hand this time.

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:14.980
You're faking an injury. That makes it worse.

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:18.070
Are those reports from the Mononokean?

00:20:18.450 --> 00:20:20.380
Just doing some research.

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:25.120
But the records have been so interesting 
since Ashiya-kun became an employee,

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:26.940
I ended up reading all of them.

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:29.370
That must be the new issue.

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:32.150
They're not magazines!

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:35.220
You came all the way here. 
Why not have some tea?

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:37.830
I have a question for you.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:42.870
A human employee?

00:20:46.040 --> 00:20:48.330
Actually, forget I asked.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:53.770
I can't guarantee this is 
related to your question,

00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:57.960
but there was an incident 
in the mundane world

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:00.230
before you were hired as an employee.

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:01.780
What incident?

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:06.190
I believe the records are at the 
Justice's White Sand Prison.

00:21:06.190 --> 00:21:09.620
Legislator, could I look at those records?

00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:12.400
That'll be difficult.

00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:15.120
The incident is classified.

00:21:15.560 --> 00:21:16.820
Classified?

00:21:17.320 --> 00:21:21.510
If I attempted to acquire those records,

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:27.230
the Justice and Executive would 
suspect something has happened.

00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:30.360
I see.

00:21:31.190 --> 00:21:32.890
White Sand Prison...

00:21:34.120 --> 00:21:39.480
is heavily guarded on the outside, 
but not so much on the inside.

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:42.730
You might be able to sneak a peek.

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:46.490
If you can sneak in, that is.

00:23:25.090 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Time: "The Cobweb"</b>

00:23:25.910 --> 00:23:27.170
Ashiya Sakae:

00:23:27.560 --> 00:23:31.290
Ashiya's father and former 
employee of the Mononokean.

00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:35.350
The more I look into him, the more
I experience an indescribable anxiety.

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:37.430
Next time, "The Cobweb."

00:23:37.430 --> 00:23:39.640
I hope nothing happens...
